    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0481" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg365"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.51/369.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Blanchard.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-07T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 2, 10 a.m. You are instructed to inform Theodore that the United
                    States will refuse to regard as legal any such issue of paper money as he
                    proposes.</p>
                <p>French and German Ambassadors in Washington have been advised in this sense, in
                    order that their nationals in Haiti may be informed. You may show this telegram
                    to your French and German colleagues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
